{
  "vibecad": "0.1",
  "name": "Base Plate",
  "material": "6061 aluminum",
  "process": "CNC or waterjet aluminum plate",
  "design_notes": "2-stage cascading Z lift (base_plate, stage1_carriage, stage2_carriage, hardware_ref, belts in lift/; assembled view lift/assembly). World: X = out of base front face, Y lateral, Z up. Stroke param s1 (0..travel) poses stage1 at +s1 and stage2 at +2*s1; every file carries s1 and the shared dims (travel, rail_spacing, rail_length, mgn_h, base_t, c1_t, zr1, drive_y, casc_x, casc_belt_y, pul_od, belt_t...). Drive: NEMA17 behind the base (shaft through a 24mm bore) at Y=drive_y; GT3 10mm loop motor pulley -> top idler (slotted for tension) on +Y side, outboard of the stage plates; stage1 clamps the inner strand. Cascade: closed GT3 loop around two idlers bolted into stage1's -Y edge; back strand clamped to the base jaw here, front strand clamped to stage2 -> stage2 moves 2x stage1 positively in both directions. Rails: HIWIN MGN9 (9x6.5, 20 pitch, M3 tapped here, depth 7). Mount: 4x M5 counterbored from the front into two horizontal 2020 extrusions behind the plate (bottom one must stop short of the motor at Y>34). Pulleys assumed GT3 20T (OD 18.34), flange OD 24.",
  "params": {
    "travel": "100 mm",
    "rail_hole_pitch": "20 mm",
    "rail_holes_count": "8",
    "nema17_bolt_spacing": "31 mm",
    "nema17_bore_d": "24 mm",
    "rail_spacing": "50 mm",
    "rail_length": "160 mm",
    "rail_hole_end": "10 mm",
    "mgn_h": "10 mm",
    "base_t": "10 mm",
    "c1_t": "10 mm",
    "x_c1": "base_t + mgn_h",
    "base_y0": "-62 mm",
    "base_w": "144 mm",
    "base_h": "210 mm",
    "zr1": "20 mm",
    "drive_y": "56 mm",
    "motor_z": "25 mm",
    "idler_z": "187 mm",
    "idler_slot_len": "10 mm",
    "belt_t": "2.41 mm",
    "belt_w": "10 mm",
    "pul_od": "18.34 mm",
    "casc_x": "x_c1 + c1_t/2",
    "casc_belt_y": "47 mm",
    "base_clamp_z": "170 mm",
    "clamp_len": "20 mm",
    "jaw_w": "20 mm",
    "jaw_screw_off": "belt_w/2 + 2.5",
    "base_jaw_t": "casc_x - pul_od/2 - belt_t - base_t"
  },
